course: dictionary
lesson: 14469
title: Participating and taking part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To participate means to take part, or join in with something. When you join a class game, you are participating. «Every child is participating in the spelling quiz today.» Participate is a more formal word for take part and join in, so you will see it in letters, rules and exams.
explain: The -ing form, participating, describes an action that is happening now. «Maya is participating in the science club.» The word shows that Maya is joining in right at this moment. Participating can also describe a group: «The participating schools will each send a team.»
explain: Ask yourself: is someone doing the activity with the others, or just watching? If they are joining in, they are participating. To check your meaning, swap in "taking part". If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Participating means taking part or joining in.
fact: «Participate» is the formal version of "take part".
fact: Participating can describe a group: «participating teams» are the teams that are taking part.
fact: «Thank you for participating» is a polite way to thank people who joined in.
fact: In a maths problem, «48 children are participating, in teams of 6»: 48 divided by 6 is 8, so there are 8 teams.
exercise: «Teachers praised everyone participating in the class discussion.» What does participating mean here? | Sitting quietly and watching | Leaving early | Forgetting about | *Taking part in
exercise: «The sports day list shows the participating schools.» Which word tells you the schools are taking part? | *participating | sports | list | schools
exercise: «48 children are participating, in teams of 6.» How many teams are there? | 6 | 42 | 54 | *8
test: «Thank you for participating» means: | Thank you for being late | Thank you for leaving early | *Thank you for taking part | Thank you for sleeping
test: In a formal letter, which phrase means the same as "take part"? | Hide from | Ask about | *Participate in | Give up on
exam: «All participating pupils will get a certificate.» What does participating tell us about the pupils? | They are late | *They are taking part | They are at home | They are asleep
